# The fixture is evidence: it must match the client's own LF line endings byte for byte.
*.log -text
sources/raw/** -text

# THE BUILT ARTIFACT IS BYTE-EXACT OR ITS NAME IS A LIE.
#
# `eqls-lockouts.<hash>.html` is named for the sha256 of its own contents —
# build-app.js hashes the exact string it then writes. So any layer that
# rewrites a byte breaks the name.
#
# Measured 1 Sep, and the round trip through git was LOSSY:
#
#   as built         309,040 B   3,849 CRLF + 50 BARE LF   -> fd053e47  (its name)
#   stored as blob   305,191 B   all LF                    -> 15f045ad
#   fresh checkout   309,090 B   3,899 CRLF, 0 bare LF     -> 41c1a2cb
#
# Normalisation folded 50 newlines that were never CRLF into CRLF on the way
# out, and they do not come back. Session A stopped its copier over exactly
# this — the artifact did not hash to its own name — and was right to.
#
# `-text` stores and restores the bytes the build produced, at every layer.
public/app/*.html -text
